422	200,876,334,1086	422. Fertile flower.	The fertile flower of the Persimmon: a small urn-shaped corolla with its lobes curled back, set in a large, leafy four-cleft calyx on a short stalk.
423	160,635,466,834	423. Corolla and stamens of the same, laid open.	The same corolla slit and spread flat: a wavy-edged band with a row of eight stamens standing on its inner face.
424	748,650,1028,1092	424. Fruit.	The Persimmon fruit: a large, smooth, plum-like berry, oval, with the four broad calyx-lobes spread under a short woody stalk at the top.
425	450,824,722,1096	425. Section of the same.	The Persimmon fruit cut across, showing the thick pulp with eight large flat seeds set in a ring round the centre.
426	1545,1355,1715,2168	426. Young spike of common Plantain.	A long, slender spike of Common Plantain, closely covered with small overlapping flowers, some near the top still buds, with fine stamens hanging from the open ones.
427	1038,1820,1296,2184	427 A flower magnified.	A single Plantain flower, magnified: a thin four-lobed corolla spread above the calyx, with four long weak filaments carrying anthers far out to the sides.
428	914,1676,1026,2168	428. Pistil of the same.	The Plantain pistil: a small egg-shaped ovary tapering into one very long, slender, hairy style.
429	1316,1818,1530,2172	429. Fruit, opening by a lid; the withered corolla on the lid.	The Plantain pod opening crosswise: the top lifted off like a lid, carrying the withered corolla with it, above the cup-shaped lower half.
